Terminals: set the selected text colour too, not just the selection

The scheme sets the selection background (OSC 17, secondary) but not the
text drawn on it, so kitty kept its configured selection_foreground, a dark
ink. On a light ArashOS theme the selection is a deep teal or blue, and that
ink on it is 2.9:1. Send onSecondary as the selection foreground (OSC 19,
which kitty and xterm support): 6.5:1 on Kaghaz, 7.8:1 on Lajvard.

--- a/src/caelestia/utils/theme.py
+++ b/src/caelestia/utils/theme.py
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@
     11: background
     12: cursor
     17: selection
+    19: selected text
     4:
         0 - 7: normal colours
         8 - 15: bright colours
@@ -98,6 +99,7 @@
         + hex_to_ansi(colours["surface"], 11)
         + hex_to_ansi(colours["secondary"], 12)
         + hex_to_ansi(colours["secondary"], 17)
+        + hex_to_ansi(colours["onSecondary"], 19)
         + hex_to_ansi(colours["term0"], 4, 0)
         + hex_to_ansi(colours["term1"], 4, 1)
         + hex_to_ansi(colours["term2"], 4, 2)
